  "solution": {
    "text": "Let in 2s body reaches upto point A and after one more second upto point B.<br /><br />Total time of ascent for a body is given as 3s<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/15192343.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 224px; height: 149px;\" /><br /><br />i.e., <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3&#160;</mn></math><math><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math> ......(i)<br /><br />Horizontal component of velocity remains always constant<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> .......(ii)<br /><br />For vertical upward motion between point O and A<br /><br /><math><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp; [Using v = u - gt]<br /><br /><math><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></math> <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Substituting this value <math> <mi>v</mi> </math> in equation (ii), we get&nbsp;<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> .....(iii)<br /><br />From equations (i) and (ii)<br /><br /><math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mtext>m&#160;s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
